== Brief Introduction

I am a PhD student in Computer Science at CDS @ HKU, fortunately advised by [https://ai.hku.hk/people/academic-staff/jpan Prof. Jia Pan]. I am interested in robot learning approaches, especially imitation learning (IL) and reinforcement learning (RL), for manipulation tasks. I was an intern at Xiaomi Robotics working on a teleoperation system with ViTai tactile sensors in 2025. I also interned at Shanghai Qizhi Institute till later in 2026, working on RL post-training for imitation robot policies.

I received the M.S. and B.S. degree in Mechanical Engineering at the School of Vehicle and Mobility from Tsinghua University in 2023 and 2020, respectively.
At THU, I was supervised by [https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Shengbo-Li-2 Prof. Shengbo Li]. I also collaborated with [http://people.iiis.tsinghua.edu.cn/~jychen/ Prof. Jianyu Chen], who leads the Intelligent System and Robotics Lab at IIIS. During my time at THU, I was interested in RL combined with optimal control, especially safe RL (where agents should not violate certain state constraints during and/or after the training process), and their applications to autonomous driving and robotics.

== News
- 07/2026: Our [https://www.science.org/doi/10.1126/scirobotics.aed6267 RL-100] paper was accepted by Science Robotics. Check the code base [https://github.com/Lei-Kun/RL-100 here].
- 10/2025: A follow-up work called [https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.12116 BiKC+] was accepted by IEEE T-ASE. Congrats to Dr. Xu and Dr. Chen!
- 08/2024: Check our WAFR 2024 paper [https://arxiv.org/abs/2406.10093 BiKC: Keypose-Conditioned Consistency Policy for Bimanual Robotic Manipulation], introducing a hierarchical policy for bimanual robotic manipulation. Congrats to all co-authors!
- 09/2023: Check our paper [https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/10329343 Safe Model-Based Reinforcement Learning with an Uncertainty-Aware Reachability Certificate] accepted by IEEE Transactions on Automation Science and Engineering. Congrats to all co-authors!
- 05/2022: Our paper [https://arxiv.org/abs/2205.07536 Reachability Constrained Reinforcement Learning] was accepted for short presentation at ICML 2022. Thank all co-authors!
